---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Investor Overview — InTellMe"
  description="InTellMe builds a checkpoint that AI systems run before they act, plus products built on the same work. Thesis, products, and how to request investor materials."
  path="/investors"
>

  <section class="room" style="padding-top:96px;padding-bottom:64px" aria-labelledby="inv-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">Investor overview</p>
      <h1 class="suite-title" id="inv-title" style="max-width:22ch">A checkpoint for AI that acts on its own, and the products built around it.</h1>
      <hr class="rule--champagne" style="margin-top:32px" />
      <p class="hero-support" style="margin-top:28px">Before an AI system acts, it should know where its information came from, whether it really comes from separate sources, and whether those sources agree. TruVector is that check. ResearchOne, SAVR, wAether and the rest of InTellMe&rsquo;s products are built on the same work.</p>
      <div class="actions" style="margin-top:36px">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="#request">Request Investor Materials</a>
        <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="#thesis">Read the thesis</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <section class="room" id="thesis" aria-labelledby="thesis-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">Thesis</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="thesis-title">Today, AI systems run on unchecked information. InTellMe is changing that.</h2>
      <div class="flagship reveal" style="margin-top:48px">
        <div class="flagship__pane">
          <p class="lede">The point is to make AI safer for everyone. Most systems still stop at generating text. The new risk is action: answers to customers, approvals, orders, filings, published posts. The risk isn&rsquo;t only that an AI says something wrong. It&rsquo;s that it acts on something wrong, and afterward nobody can tell what it was relying on.</p>
          <p>Most AI tooling works on producing better answers. Almost nothing sits between the information and the action and leaves a record someone can review afterward.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flagship__pane">
          <p>InTellMe builds that checkpoint. Before an AI acts, it checks the information behind the action and answers Allow, Review, or Block, with the reasons attached.</p>
          <p>The other products apply the same discipline to everyday tools.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="room room--alt" id="ships" aria-labelledby="ships-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">Active projects</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="ships-title">Core technology, then commercial ventures.</h2>

      <ul class="rail reveal" style="margin-top:48px">
        <li>
          <div class="product__meta" style="margin-bottom:8px">
            <span class="rail__name">Lane Vector</span>
          </div>
          <span class="rail__note">Research program: bookkeeping from chemical kinetics applied to how information moves, where the transfer is derived (direction, rate-estimate noise floor, source independence, stiffness as a numerical problem). Copies do not conserve; there is no K_eq for public belief. Papers at lanevector.com.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="product__meta" style="margin-bottom:8px">
            <span class="rail__name">TruVector</span>
          </div>
          <span class="rail__note">A checkpoint an AI system runs before it acts. It answers Allow, Review, or Block, with the reasons attached. More at <a href="https://truvector.science" rel="noopener">truvector.science</a>.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="product__meta" style="margin-bottom:8px">
            <span class="rail__name">ResearchOne</span>
          </div>
          <span class="rail__note">A research workspace that keeps every source attached, keeps disagreements visible, and shows how each conclusion was reached.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="product__meta" style="margin-bottom:8px">
            <span class="rail__name">SAVR</span>
          </div>
          <span class="rail__note">AI-assisted kitchen inventory and recipe planning that turns what you already have into meals.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="product__meta" style="margin-bottom:8px">
            <span class="rail__name">Golden Goose Tools</span>
          </div>
          <span class="rail__note">Small tools you buy and keep. BugNote and a technical SEO audit are live.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="product__meta" style="margin-bottom:8px">
            <span class="rail__name">Golden Goose Tees Studio</span>
          </div>
          <span class="rail__note">Design your own shirt with AI, see it on a mockup, and order it printed and shipped, at goldengoosetees.com.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="product__meta" style="margin-bottom:8px">
            <span class="rail__name">wAether</span>
          </div>
          <span class="rail__note">A public observatory of solar, galactic, and terrestrial telemetry on official government data sources. Pricing starts at $4.99/month or $49.99/year.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="room" id="funding" aria-labelledby="fund-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">Investment</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="fund-title">Self-funded so far. Raising a pre-seed round.</h2>
      <p class="reveal" style="margin-top:22px;max-width:62ch">InTellMe has been built without outside money. The round will pay for:</p>
      <ul class="reveal">
        <li>TruVector research and development</li>
        <li>Growing ResearchOne and SAVR</li>
        <li>Company operations</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="reveal" style="margin-top:22px;max-width:62ch">Terms, structure and financials are in the investor materials.</p>
      <div class="actions reveal" style="margin-top:24px">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="#request">Request investor materials</a>
        <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="#request">Request the TruVector Technical Brief</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="room room--alt" id="founder" aria-labelledby="founder-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">Founder</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="founder-title">Built by Michael Brandon Lane.</h2>
      <div class="flagship reveal" style="margin-top:40px">
        <div class="flagship__pane">
          <p class="lede">InTellMe is an independent research and software company founded and operated by Michael Brandon Lane, a chemical engineer and chemist based in Johnson City, Tennessee.</p>
          <p>Before InTellMe, Lane worked at Celgard on lithium-ion battery separator and coating technology, including the development and scale-up of coated separator systems for high-volume manufacturing. He is a named inventor on multiple Celgard patents covering coated battery separators, including <a href="https://patents.google.com/patent/US11949124B2/en" rel="noopener">U.S. Patent 11,949,124</a>.</p>
          <p>That work shaped how he builds software: <strong>every number should trace back to a measurement, uncertainty should be stated out loud, and conclusions should change when the data does.</strong> The same discipline now applies to systems that check information instead of materials.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flagship__pane">
          <p>Product sites are listed on the main page. A short line from a decision to a shipped change is the operating point.</p>
          <ul class="facts">
            <li>Direct &mdash; <a href="mailto:info@intellmeai.com">info@intellmeai.com</a></li>
            <li><a href="tel:+17473221977">(747) 322-1977</a></li>
            <li>Johnson City, Tennessee</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="room" id="request" aria-labelledby="request-title">
    <div class="suite">
      <p class="kicker">Request</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="request-title">Request investor materials.</h2>
      <p class="reveal" style="margin-top:20px;max-width:56ch">The deck, technical briefs, roadmap, use of funds, IP summary, and demo access are sent after review. Nothing is attached automatically.</p>

      <form class="form reveal" id="investor-form" method="post" action="/api/investor-request">
        <input type="hidden" name="_started" id="_started" value="" />
        <div class="hp" aria-hidden="true">
          <label for="company_website">Company website</label>
          <input type="text" id="company_website" name="company_website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
        </div>

        <div class="field">
          <label for="name">Name <span class="req">(required)</span></label>
          <input type="text" id="name" name="name" required autocomplete="name" />
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="email">Email <span class="req">(required)</span></label>
          <input type="email" id="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email" />
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="organization">Organization</label>
          <input type="text" id="organization" name="organization" autocomplete="organization" />
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="role">Role</label>
          <input type="text" id="role" name="role" autocomplete="organization-title" />
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="want">What you are looking for</label>
          <select id="want" name="want">
            <option value="Technical brief">Technical brief</option>
            <option value="Investor materials" selected>Investor materials</option>
            <option value="Demo access">Demo access</option>
            <option value="Other">Other</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="found">How you found InTellMe</label>
          <input type="text" id="found" name="found" />
        </div>
        <div class="field field--wide">
          <label for="message">Message</label>
          <textarea id="message" name="message" rows="5"></textarea>
        </div>

        <div class="field--wide actions" style="margin-top:8px">
          <button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit">Send request</button>
          <span class="caption">Or write directly to <a href="mailto:info@intellmeai.com?subject=Investor%20materials">info@intellmeai.com</a>.</span>
        </div>
      </form>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  .form { display: grid; gap: 24px 32px; margin-top: 40px; max-width: 720px; }
  @media (min-width: 768px) { .form { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
  .field { display: grid; gap: 8px; }
  .field--wide { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  .form label {
    font-family: var(--label); font-weight: 500; font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--stone-text);
  }
  .req { letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: none; color: var(--stone-text); }
  .form input, .form select, .form textarea {
    width: 100%;
    background: var(--smoked-bronze);
    color: var(--ivory);
    border: 1px solid var(--bronze-edge);
    border-radius: 1px;
    padding: 13px 14px;
    font-family: var(--body); font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.4;
    min-height: 44px;
    transition: border-color var(--t-micro) var(--ease-lobby);
  }
  .form textarea { min-height: 120px; resize: vertical; }
  .form input:hover, .form select:hover, .form textarea:hover { border-color: var(--bronze-edge-hot); }
  .form input:user-invalid, .form textarea:user-invalid {
    border-color: var(--danger);
    box-shadow: inset 3px 0 0 var(--danger);
  }
  .hp { position: absolute; left: -9999px; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; }
</style>

<script src="/form-timing.js" defer is:inline></script>
